WEBVTT

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.790
Goodbye...

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.600
How is it, Keiichirou?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.110
Yes, no doubt, that’s the signal of a Mew Aqua.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:50.800
But...

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.320
It’s weak.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.350
Yes.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:57.020
It looks like it’s moving slowly.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.790
Where’s the last confirmed location?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.310
Latitude 45 degrees North,
longitude 155 degrees East.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.850
It was moving south by sea, near the Chishima Islands.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.360
Judging from its speed, it can’t be an airplane.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.440
Maybe a ship?

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.090
I thought so. The estimated destination is Tokyo.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.580
This is going to be troublesome...

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:20.000
We can’t inspect all cargo.
There are too many ships in Tokyo Bay.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:23.200
<i>WHAAAT?!?!</i>

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.660
Geez, what’s with all the noise?

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.500
What a surprise!

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.960
This is news!

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.250
This can’t be true!

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:29.740
This can’t be true!

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.840
But it’s clearly written in here.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.880
I will NEVER believe that!

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.350
Well... Yeah...

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.240
I guess there must be some kind of mistake.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.270
Sure! This is just ridiculous.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.600
But, Zakuro-san is so popular.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.230
What’s that got to do with this!?

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.960
What’s going on in here?

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.070
Oh, it looks like everyone gathered here.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.420
Did something happen?

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.500
This is super-duper huge news!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.350
Hollywood has offered her a leading role in a movie.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.560
“Is Fujiwara Zakuro going to move to Los Angeles?”

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.520
She is really multi-talented.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.550
Zakuro-oneechan is going to America?

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.170
Bu-Ling, that hasn’t been decided yet.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.650
Zakuro hasn’t told us anything yet.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.150
WRONG! No smoke without fire!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.020
Probably...

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:35.860
She’s probably going to become a
top baseball player in America!

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.930
Bu-Ling-san, Zakuro-san is not
going there to play baseball.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.380
I know, I was just making a joke about America, I thought it’d be fun.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.880
...I hope you enjoyed it!

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.590
Anyway, let’s ask Zakuro-san once she gets here.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.480
Ok, Minto?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.390
I...

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.010
Oneesama!

00:02:59.010 --> 00:02:59.850
Um...

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.030
Zakuro-san, is this article for real?

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:11.070
Ah that, yes, the movie offer is true,

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.440
but I haven’t decided yet what to do.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:15.880
Oneesama!

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.580
Yes, Minto?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.510
I will go with you to America!

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.030
Wait a minute Minto, what are you talking about?

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.350
It’d be pointless for me to stay here
in Japan without you, Oneesama!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:31.370
Don’t be silly...

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:35.220
Oneesama, I beg you, take me with you!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.670
Wahh, that’s the breaking up of Tokyo Mew Mew!

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.240
Why should that happen?

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.100
How can we beat the aliens if Zakuro-
oneechan and Minto-oneechan are missing?

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.810
Bu-Ling doesn’t wanna lose.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.020
Hey, Bu-Ling!
What’re you talking about...

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.020
...now,

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.670
...geez...

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:54.830
Enough!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.380
We’ve gone through a lot of fights,

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.880
but you still don’t understand what it means to save the Earth, do you?

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.550
Oneesama?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.510
Zakuro-san...?

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.310
Honestly, I’ve run out of patience.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:14.070
I haven’t decided yet what to do about that job,

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:19.700
but that doesn’t mean that the possibility of going is zero.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.270
Listen, Minto!

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.620
You are not an actress
nor part of our staff.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.550
I have no reason to take you with me.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.940
This is indeed bad timing.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.810
Bad timing?

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.040
We got a signal from a Mew Aqua.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.740
Everyone, come downstairs.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.110
I’ve found you, Quiche!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.180
You guys.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.620
What were you just looking at?

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.490
I’ve just received some news from our planet.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.700
Environmental conditions are becoming worse.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.620
If we don’t hurry...

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:26.490
Quiche, we have a signal from a Mew Aqua.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.720
Deep Blue-sama ordered us to obtain it.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.620
Huh, he’s so arrogant.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.080
Hey, Quiche, you better be careful what you say!

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.230
Whatever. Deep Blue hates me
anyway, so I couldn’t care less.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.270
Everyone at home is just waiting and waiting,

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:46.520
for the day when Deep Blue awakens to come save them.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:48.760
But how do we get there?

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.570
“Extinguish humans!” “Get the Mew Aqua!”
He’s just ordering us around,

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:55.150
without giving a damn for the people on our planet!

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.210
What on Earth does he want?

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.480
Your wound seems to have healed well, if you are fine enough to bitch around like that.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.680
But we cannot cooperate with someone
who doesn’t agree with our plan.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.330
We’ll go look for the Mew Aqua.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.660
You stay here for a while.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.920
Do whatever you want.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:17.080
Quiche...

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:17.900
What?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.180
It’s not only you...

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.070
...who cares about the others back home.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.950
Somewhere in Tokyo Bay?

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.730
Yes. It could be on an cruise ship, or a fishing boat.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.280
Anyway, I bet the Mew Aqua is in with some cargo.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:48.110
Let’s call the captain of each ship, one after another!

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.700
No, that wouldn’t work.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.240
As you can see in the case of that Christmas tree,

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:56.170
a Mew Aqua can reside anywhere.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:03.420
So, unless its power is released, even
the one who carries it won’t notice it.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.880
Hmm, I’m totally clueless!

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.470
Why didn’t you tell me that we are going
out before I changed clothes?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.820
Zakuro-san?

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:13.680
What’s wrong?

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.480
I’m still a Mew Mew.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:23.260
The only way to find it is to go to the harbour and wait for it to react with one of us.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:27.740
But a Mew Aqua only reacts when something happens, like when your emotions run high.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.360
Is there any other way?

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.790
Um... No.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.580
We’ll keep on doing the analysis here.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.290
Anyway, everyone go to the harbour.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.270
I’m relying on all of you.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.730
Let’s split up to look for the signal. Ok?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.490
If anyone finds anything, contact the rest of us.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.190
Fine!

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.310
Minto?

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:53.860
Minto...

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.330
How’s it going?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.990
The distance is too short.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.810
We can’t locate it because the signals are coming from everywhere.

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:01.580
After all,

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.540
we have to wait until someone gets near the Mew Aqua to feel a reaction in her body.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:13.410
Ahh, can I really find it...?

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.510
Ichigo, don’t give up, don’t give up!

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.470
Oh, Masha, you’re so lucky!

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:24.680
Bu-Ling-san, what are you doing?

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:28.290
I can’t just wait for my body to shine.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:29.960
I’m trying to smell it out!

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:33.140
Bu-Ling-san, you know how a Mew Aqua smells?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.180
Actually, no, I don’t.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.950
Let’s go look for it in a normal way then...

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.740
Oneesama...

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.660
Are you really going?!

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.810
Any comments to the fans in Japan?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.280
<i>To my dear Zakuro:</i>

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:13.720
<i>Time does fly.</i>

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.740
<i>It’s been almost two years since you left home.</i>

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.020
<i>Are you doing well?</i>

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.030
<i>We don’t know if you ever forgave
us for what happened back then.</i>

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:31.160
<i>Yet, we’re waiting for your return, whenever it might be.</i>

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:35.540
Why? Why didn’t you believe me?

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:38.120
WHY?!

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:49.680
What’s that?

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.010
Who’s there?

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:57.290
Heh, I found a Mew Mew!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.480
It seems we’re both looking for the same thing.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.980
Tell me where the Mew Aqua is!

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:14.880
Ryou, that is...

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.330
As I feared, they have detected it, too.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.730
Ichigo! The aliens have showed up!

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:20.550
Near Zakuro!

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.260
Transform and head there!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.620
Ok!

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.720
Minto, did you hear it too?

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.080
What is it? I was thinking...

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.690
<i>The aliens appeared where Zakuro is!</i>

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.190
Oneesama!? Then we need to hurry!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.690
Now, let’s go everyone!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:35.320
Yes.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.400
Ok!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.270
Mew Mew Lettuce METAMORPHO-SE!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.450
Mew Mew Pudding METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:07.000
Mew Mew Mint METAMORPHO-SE!

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:21.520
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.370
What? You’re not going to transform?

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.690
Where is the Mew Aqua?

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.290
We know it has to be somewhere around here.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:17.080
If you want it that much,
why don’t you look for it yourself?

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.500
It’s too much to ask a stranger to do it for you.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:23.720
What? You’re way too cocky!

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.460
S-Say something!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.690
Do you hear me?
You’re scaring me now!

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.880
What are they doing?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.110
Zakuro-san!

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:41.690
Zakuro-san!

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.570
Oneesama!

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.240
Zakuro-oneechan, hurry and transform!

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:50.700
Oneesama?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.380
What’s the matter with Zakuro?

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:53.380
Zakuro-san!

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:59.840
I’ll decide whether
I’m going to fight or not.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.800
What do you mean? I don’t understand...

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.200
I don’t really get it, but it looks
like a problem between allies.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.760
Well if so, let’s go ahead and attack.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.220
Fuu Rai Sen!

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.920
Ho Rai Kyu!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.060
Go, Parapara!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:19.890
Oh no...

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.270
LettasTanets.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.750
Reborn Lettuce Rush!

00:13:40.890 --> 00:13:42.220
PuddingRings!

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:50.260
Reborn PuddingRings Inferno!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.730
Didn’t work!

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.730
Look out!

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.830
Reborn Mint Echo!

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.820
Kannin, kannin! (Forgive me!)

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.090
Oneesama!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:30.390
Oneesama?!

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:32.800
Why...

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.180
Why won’t you transform and fight?

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:38.140
I’m sorry, but I can’t.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:45.490
But why...? Oneesama?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.860
Where is the Mew Aqua?

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.030
Even if I knew, I wouldn’t tell you!

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.790
You girls, just tell me where you’re hiding it!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.460
Like I said earlier, even though you are my friend, I will punish you if you do bad things!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.920
Why would I be your friend?

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:04.800
Look out!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.220
Minto!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.170
Damn you...!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:29.000
Reborn Strawberry Surprise!

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:36.330
I said Kannin...!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.370
Darn, one more!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.380
Wait!

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:41.830
What?

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:45.040
It looks like they really don’t know where it is.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.580
Let’s stop this useless fight.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.590
Minto, hang in there!

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.550
Minto-san!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.260
Minto-oneechan!

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.310
Heh.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:09.190
Um, Shirogane, there must be a reason
why Zakuro-san didn’t fight today!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:13.030
So... Ok, what should I say...

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.580
What’s going on?

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.620
Is he scolding her?

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.620
Being so sneaky is bad.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:24.210
I mean...

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.130
Ahh, um, well... I’m sorry...

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:30.500
I couldn’t hear anything!
I mean, I also didn’t mean to...

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:31.210
Ichigo...

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.050
Yes?

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.760
Take care of Minto, please.

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.300
Occasionally she is under
severe stress,

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.390
because she worries too much
about the future.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.980
It’s you who has to offer her
support now.

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:46.100
Zakuro-san.

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:50.900
Everyone,

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.530
I’m sorry about calling all of you in so early.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:55.490
Akasaka-san, Zakuro-san isn’t here yet.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:17:00.450
Is that so? Even though I contacted her,
I didn’t get an answer.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:01.950
Unbelievable.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.910
Just what is going on with her?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:08.960
Mail, mail! You’ve got a mail!

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.970
Masha, what is it?

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:14.890
It’s from Zakuro!

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:19.350
<i>We only had a short time together.</i>

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:21.730
<i>But I enjoyed it.</i>

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.100
Th-That means...!

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.440
Zakuro-oneechan really quit!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.900
We should go look for her immediately!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:29.560
Stop it already.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.940
Shirogane...

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.780
If she doesn’t want to fight then
we shouldn’t force her to.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:35.860
How can you...

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:37.240
Why not?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.240
Listen!

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.700
Zakuro didn’t help Mew Mint when she was in danger.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.870
The fights against the aliens will
be even harder in the future.

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.870
If we get distracted, even for a moment, we can’t win.

00:17:51.870 --> 00:17:54.880
If we lose, the Earth will fall into their hands!

00:17:58.630 --> 00:17:59.840
Ridiculous...

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:00.800
What?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.470
You’re ridiculous!

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:04.100
Ichigo-san...?

00:18:03.380 --> 00:18:05.350
Everyone gets that feeling of being lost sometimes!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.150
Everyone faces problems every day, and
you don’t know what to do about them!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.400
But everyone is still trying their best to solve them.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.650
So if Zakuro is in this kind of situation
now, we have to be there for her!

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:17.370
If you say I mustn’t hesitate at all I can’t fight either!

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:21.620
Neither could Minto,
Retasu, nor Bu-Ling!

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.330
There’s no reason to discuss that now.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.290
Zakuro is the one who decided.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.660
What are you talking about?

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:33.000
What I’m saying is that you shouldn’t be so hard on her!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.510
After all, you are the one who forced us to
join the Mew Project, aren’t you, Shirogane?

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:38.680
So, will you quit too?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.180
Why? No, I won’t,

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.720
but I do have my own opinion of what needs to be done!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.400
Minto, let’s go find Zakuro.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:48.690
Minto?

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.980
If she quits, I don’t know what to do.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:53.690
Minto...?

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.490
What can we do? What can we do now?

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:02.080
I believe in Zakuro-san,
I’m sure she’ll come back!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:03.660
Ichigo...

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.490
Hey-ey, Ichigo!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.290
We’ll join them too!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.250
Ichigo-oneechan can be really pushy sometimes.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.210
Masha too, Masha too!

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:20.340
You said we should look for her, but
do you have any idea where she is?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.930
Let’s see..

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.060
Minto, any idea where she could be?

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.860
Eh?! I...

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.510
Masha knows!

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:29.980
What, really, Masha?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:47.870
Yo!

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.670
Oneesama?

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.510
Zakuro-san!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:07.140
Oneesama...?

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.360
Zakuro-san...?

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.180
Oneesama, why didn’t you save me?

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:31.760
Oneesama, you would have let me die without helping!

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:32.820
Why?

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:34.480
Why is that?

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:40.220
Oneesama, you left us and...
you’re going to Quiche now?

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:41.030
No way!

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.600
<i>Honestly, I’ve run out of patience.</i>

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.700
Please wait, Oneesama!

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:49.110
Next: “Friend or Foe? Fight, Oneesama!”

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:53.420
If I lose you, Oneesama, I’ll...!
